WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:04.740
So this is Mercury. It’s a liquid metal,
it is one of the, well,

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.729
one liquid metal at this temperature. There
are a couple of

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:10.500
liquid metals in a little bit more exotic
places in the world like

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.719
Spain or perhaps Africa. But mercury is the
chemical formula

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:19.199
Hg, the best way to remember the formula for
mercury is like

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:22.109
H.G. Wells. Hg, mercury, comes out of a well.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:26.760
Mercury is one of the few elements that is
liquid at room

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.470
temperature or is the only metal that is liquid
at room

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.180
temperature unless you live in a very hot
country, it is also

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.610
very dense. And it has been known again since
very early

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.060
times. Mercury is very poisonous.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.180
It is a really fantastic liquid. It was really
used for making

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.460
scientific instruments like barometers and
thermometers, you

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.000
know, and it’s really quite a beautiful
metal. I really love it,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.020
when I was in school we used to but it on
the bench and play

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.120
football with it. You know, lots of people
don’t like us to do

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.780
that anymore, but what I will do is to pour
a little bit of the

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.890
liquid metal into this beaker so we can see
the properties and

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.520
you can see that it is really nice. Flows,
just like a liquid, it

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.530
forms really quite nice balls. And you can
see the really quite

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.970
high meniscus forming around the mercury.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.840
It can get into the human body particularly
in the brain where

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:25.760
it gives signs of madness. It used to be used
in the UK for

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.700
making hats. I am not quite sure what they
did with mercury

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.390
to make hats, but this is where the expression,
“mad as a

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:37.530
hatter” came from, because the people making
hats breathed

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.990
in mercury vapour and this caused them to
show signs of

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.030
madness.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.330
So here we can slosh it around a little bit
but we have got to

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.850
be very careful that we don’t slosh it too
much because it is

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.040
extremely dense and heavy and it is very,
very easy to go

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.890
through the middle or the bottom of the glass
bottle itself.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.240
Tell me why you aren’t touching it with
your hands?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.900
Well mercury it is associated with toxicity
especially for the

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.110
salts, so you know we like to try and minimise
the contact

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.600
with the mercury and the mercury salts as
much as possible

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.080
really, just so that we could be very careful
with our health

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.080
and safety.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.920
There was a tragic case in Japan in the 1950s,
when mercury

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:21.230
got into the sea from chemical emissions from
factories, and

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:25.490
the organisms on the bottom of the sea turned
them into,

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.100
the mercury metal, into a compound that could
be absorbed

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:34.730
by the fish, particularly the shellfish, and
then the fishermen

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.420
and the people living the round this Minamata
Bay, starting

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.990
eating these things got large amounts of mercury
in their

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:46.080
brain. And I can’t remember the number but
several thousand

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.130
people got very ill and many of them died,
so mercury in the

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:54.080
environment is quite a serious problem. It
is also an

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:59.790
interesting point that mercury has been used
for making

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.960
chlorine by putting electric current thought
solutions of salt

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:09.140
and it is gradually being replaced. But unlike
chemicals you

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.630
can’t get rid of an element, so if you have
mercury you can’t

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:18.080
burn it or destroy it in any way. And so,
there are problems

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.610
now, what to do with the mercury that people
no longer

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.610
want.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:24.890
But it is a really beautiful element, really
fantastic. It is used

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.260
very often in electric chemistry, because
you can form very,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.820
very good electrical contact with mercury.
And in fact, many

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.261
people that may have old telephones or old
bells, you know

00:03:35.261 --> 00:03:38.600
the door bells which we have on our front
door, inside the

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.790
‘bing-bong’, is a mercury-activated switch
which turns on the

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:46.530
magnet and off the magnet very, very quickly.
It is really

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.530
beautiful.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.680
Mercury has an interesting property that it
will very easily

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.630
form alloys which are called amalgams. My
teeth and probably

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.740
many of your teeth are filled with so called
silver amalgam

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:05.270
which is a mixture of mercury and silver which
when it is

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.910
freshly mixed is like a paste. But when the
dentist pushes it

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:13.230
into your tooth it then hardens and, all being
well, it does not

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.520
come out or at least does not come out for
a number of

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.730
years. But amalgams are not very strong. And
many years

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:27.690
ago when I worked at another university, mercury
was being

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:31.720
stolen from the university, from the chemistry
department

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:36.290
and nobody knew who was stealing it. Until
one day the

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.070
window cleaner was walking out of the building
and the

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:43.780
bottom fell out of his bucket, because he
had been stealing

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.230
mercury by pouring it into the bottom…pouring
it into his

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:52.720
bucket and hiding it below the dirty water.
And the mercury

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.640
started to amalgamate with the metal of the
bucket, it was a

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.370
metal bucket, and eventually, the bucket could
no longer hold

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.270
the weight of the mercury and it suddenly
fell out and the

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:04.900
mercury all came off.

